{"name":"Western Reserve","hex":"#8d876d","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"western","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, facing, situated in, or related to the west.","Of a wind, blowing from the west; westerly."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["(Should we move, merge or split this sense?)  A film, or some other dramatic work, set in, the historic (c. 1850–1910) American West (west of the Mississippi river) focusing on conflict between whites and Indians, lawmen and outlaws, ranchers and farmers, or industry (railroads, mining) and agriculture."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/western"},{"term":"reserve","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A restriction.\nThe act of reserving or keeping back; reservation; exception.","The act of reserving or keeping back; reservation; exception."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To keep back; to retain.","To keep in store for future or special use."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reserve"}],"entries":[{"title":"Connecticut Western Reserve","blocks":[{"text":"The Connecticut Western Reserve was a portion of land claimed by the Connecticut Colony and later state of Connecticut in what is now mostly Northeast Ohio. The Western Reserve had been granted to Connecticut under the terms of its colonial charter by Charles II of England. The county seat of the Western Reserve was Warren, Ohio."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Ctwestclaims.png/330px-Ctwestclaims.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Connecticut_Western_Reserve"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Western_Reserve_Including_the_Fire_Lands_1826.jpg/500px-Western_Reserve_Including_the_Fire_Lands_1826.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Western_Res